# Python project structure

Keep a layered layout. Do not dump endpoints, business logic, and models in one file.

```
app/
  main.py           # FastAPI app factory and router includes only
  config.py         # Settings (env, pydantic-settings). No business logic.
  constants.py      # Domain constants and enums. No I/O.
  exceptions.py     # Custom exceptions and exception handlers
  {feature}/
    route.py        # HTTP layer: path ops, status codes, Depends
    service.py      # Business logic and orchestration
    schemas.py      # Pydantic request/response models
tests/
  {feature}/
    test_*.py
```

## File rules

- `route.py`: parse request, call service, map exceptions to HTTP. No business rules.
- `service.py`: all business logic. Never import FastAPI `Request`/`Response`.
- `schemas.py`: Pydantic models only. No DB or HTTP calls.
- `config.py`: one `Settings` class. Read env here, nowhere else.
- `constants.py`: magic strings/numbers live here, not inline in routes/services.
- `exceptions.py`: typed domain errors. Routes translate them to HTTP.

## Do not

- Put Pydantic models inside `route.py` or `service.py`.
- Call the database or external APIs from `route.py`.
- Create a new top-level module that duplicates these roles.
